# .env.staging / .env.production are deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# Every value in them is either VITE_-prefixed — which Vite bakes into the
# client bundle and therefore serves to every visitor — or the publishable
# Supabase anon key under a second name. None of it is secret, and keeping it
# out of the repo cost more than it protected: Cloudflare's Workers Builds
# could never build (both PR checks failed on every PR, so a red check stopped
# meaning anything), and every fresh clone or git worktree silently produced a
# bundle with an empty Supabase URL.
#
# NEVER put a service-role key, a Square access token, or any other real secret
# in these files. Server-side secrets belong in Supabase function secrets
# (`supabase secrets set`), which is also the only place they work.


# Supabase CLI local state (linked project ref, version caches)
supabase/.temp/

# Claude Code's own state — session transcripts, caches, and the git worktrees
# other sessions are working in. It reached 187 MB / ~2,900 files in the shared
# checkout, which buried real changes in `git status` and is how a pile of
# macOS " 2"/" 3" copy artifacts went unnoticed long enough to be mistaken for
# work.
.claude/

# Deno's lockfile for the edge functions. No deno.lock has ever been tracked
# here, and the functions deploy through the Supabase CLI rather than CI, so it
# pins nothing anyone else consumes. Committing stray lockfiles has bitten this
# repo before: a stale bun.lock took the Cloudflare build off npm and made the
# PR checks fail on every PR (c7ac00b).
deno.lock
